gent team to get help on manual re-installation. From a working VM, copy the installer .zip file from path C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot<LatestVersion Copy it to affected VM at path C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot<LatestVersion Unzip the .zip file contents (with replace all option) at same folder (C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot<LatestVersion ) Open command prompt (as admin) and run below commands - REG ADD "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\BcdrAgent" /v IsProviderInstalled /t REG SZ /d False /f - cd C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot\1.0.71.0 - IaaSBcdrExtension.exe install And copy it to affected VM at path C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot<LatestVersion REG ADD "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\BcdrAgent" /v IsProviderInstalled /t REG SZ /d False /f cd C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot\1.0.71.0 IaaSBcdrExtension.exe install 排查思路 union cluster('mabprod1').database('MABKustoProd1').TraceLogMessage, cluster('mabprodweu').database('MABKustoProd').TraceLogMessage, cluster('mabprodwus').database('MABKustoProd').TraceLogMessage To Check if Subscription of customer has undergone Tenant Migration: EventLog TraceLogMessage Step 5: Validate if the CMK Update succeeds in the Jobs page. Step 6: After the previous step is complete, re-trigger the backups and check if it succeeds. Step 4: Validate if the CMK Update succeeds in the Jobs page. Step 5: After the previous step is complete, re-trigger the backups and check if it succeeds. Trigger backup from Portal 操作步骤 / 命令 未从原文中明确识别。 关键参数 / 状态码 未从原文中明确识别。 根因 / 结论 How to verify if the failure is caused by this specific root cause? Root cause 3: VMSnapshot Extension may have been manually uninstalled 解决方案 What is the workaround? If the Subscription (with Recovery service vault, the data source protected say IaaS VM, and key vault used for CMK) are all migrated to new tenant, then the backups on CMK enabled vault might fail with the error BCMProtGetSaSUriAsyncError. What is the workaround? To resolve this issue, follow the steps listed below on each of the impacted vaults Solution 1: If the System Assigned Identity is used in Recovery Services Vault Step 1: Disable the Vault System Assigned MSI Step 2: Re-enable the Vault System Assigned MSI Solution 2: If the user Assigned Identity is used in Recovery Services Vault: 参考链接 Execute: [Web] [Desktop] [Web (Lens)] [Desktop (SAW)] 原始内容清洗稿（保留备查） What is the customer facing symptom for this failure? Backup failure with ErrorCode BCMProtGetSaSUriAsyncError Cause 1: Insufficient permissions for the Recovery services vault to access Azure Key Vault How to verify if the failure is caused by this specific root cause? If below query results in some rows as output : Plain Text union cluster('mabprod1').database('MABKustoProd1').TraceLogMessage, cluster('mabprodweu').database('MABKustoProd').TraceLogMessage, cluster('mabprodwus').database('MABKustoProd').TraceLogMessage where TIMESTAMP ago(20d) where TaskId == "<TaskId " project PreciseTimeStamp, ServiceName, FileNameLineNumber, Message, Level = Level + 1, TaskId where Message contains "UserErrorProtCMKAKVAuthFailure" What is the workaround? Follow below documentation to provide KeyVault having Customer Managed Key (CMK) access to the RecoveryService Vault Encryption of backup data using customer-managed keys Customer Ready Content Cause 2: The Subscription is migrated to new tenant If the Subscription (with Recovery service vault, the data source protected say IaaS VM, and key vault used for CMK) are all migrated to new tenant, then the backups on CMK enabled vault might fail with the error BCMProtGetSaSUriAsyncError. To Check if Subscription of customer has undergone Tenant Migration: Step1 Execute: [Web] [Desktop] [Web (Lens)] [Desktop (SAW)] EventLog where TIMESTAMP ago(60d) where StampName == "eus-pod01-rrp1" where EventCode == 5020 where