y - User Assigned - Remove the identity used under CMK settings. Step 2: Re-add the same User Assigned Identity to RS Vault Navigate to 'Vault' - Identity - User Assigned - Add the identity used under CMK settings. Step 3: Save and Re-apply CMK with the same settings Step 4: Validate if the CMK Update succeeds in the Jobs page. Step 5: After the previous step is complete, re-trigger the backups and check if it succeeds. Root cause 3: VMSnapshot Extension may have been manually uninstalled CSI incident for which this TSG is created Incident 271853625 : [Waiting on CSS]CRITSIT [IAASVM],[BACKUPFAIL],[ONLINE] [arnoel] [Backup failed with GA issue after migrating to new tenant Error code I am seeing "BCMProtGetSaSUriAsyncError"] ErrorCode GuestAgentSnapshotTaskStatusError ErrorCode GuestAgentSnapshotTaskStatusError for Windows VM If Extension was manually uninstalled (although it is never advisable to do that) Please try below steps to manually install back the VMSnapshot extension. If it does not work, please reach-out to Guest-Agent team to get help on manual re-installation. From a working VM, copy the installer .zip file from path C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot<LatestVersion Copy it to affected VM at path C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot<LatestVersion Unzip the .zip file contents (with replace all option) at same folder (C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot<LatestVersion ) Open command prompt (as admin) and run below commands REG ADD "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\BcdrAgent" /v IsProviderInstalled /t REG SZ /d False /f cd C:\Packages\Plugins\Microsoft.Azure.RecoveryServices.VMSnapshot\1.0.71.0 IaaSBcdrExtension.exe install Trigger backup f
